---
config: tests/fresco_batch.config
args: --fresco
---

The default contextual prelude supplies collections without extra paths
(map(fun(x) { x+1 },[40,41]),Just(42) : Maybe(Int))
stdout : ([41, 42], Just(42)) : (List Int, [|Just:Int|Nothing|])

An explicit later prelude import uses its qualified aliases
open import FrescoPrelude; var x=(Just(42) : FrescoPrelude.Maybe(Int)); switch(x) { case Just(n) -> n case Nothing -> 0 }
stdout : 42 : Int

An explicit custom prelude supplies values and persistent fixities
(seed+2,10 +++ 3 +++ 1)
args : --fresco --set=prelude=tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/customPrelude.links
stdout : prelude:tail:(42, 8) : (Int, Int)

An explicit empty prelude keeps the primitive only environment
map(fun(x) { x+1 },[41])
args : --fresco --set=prelude=tests/empty_prelude.links
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error: Unbound variable map.*

A custom prelude error stops before user evaluation
print("user must not execute")
args : --fresco --set=prelude=tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/invalidPrelude.links
exit : 1
stdout : @^$
stderr : @.*invalidPrelude.links:1: Type error:.*

Typecheck only mode checks the custom prelude and source without evaluation
tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/check.links
filemode : true
args : --fresco --set=typecheck_only=true --set=prelude=tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/customPrelude.links --set=recheck_frontend_transformations=true
stdout : @^$

Canonical bootstrap and diamond imports share one effect identity and evaluation
tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/diamond.links
filemode : true
args : --fresco --enable-handlers --set=stdlib_path=tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/stdlib --path=tests/fixtures/fresco_batch
stdout : once:42 : Int

Shared batch inputs retain bootstrap identity and evaluate expressions before files
tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/persistent.links
filemode : true
args : --fresco --set=isolation=false --set=stdlib_path=tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/stdlib -e "var saved=40; saved"
stdout : @once:40 : Int\n42 : Int$

Isolated batch inputs retain the initial prelude and discard earlier definitions
tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/persistent.links
filemode : true
args : --fresco --set=stdlib_path=tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/stdlib -e "var saved=40; saved"
exit : 1
stdout : once:40 : Int
stderr : @.*Type error: Unbound variable saved.*

The explicit legacy selector retains the legacy default prelude
var old=(fun() { 42 } : () ~> Int); hd(map(fun(x) { x },[42]))
args : --fresco --set=fresco=false
stdout : 42 : Int

A missing explicit prelude stops before user evaluation
print("user must not execute")
args : --fresco --set=prelude=tests/fixtures/fresco_batch/missingPrelude.links
exit : 1
stdout : @^$
stderr : @.*Sys_error.*missingPrelude.links.*
